            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-55380",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "python-pillow: Pillow: Denial of Service via crafted GD 2.x image file"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Pillow is a Python imaging library. Prior to 12.3.0, PIL/GdImageFile.py GdImageFile._open() read image dimensions from the GD 2.x header and stored them in self._size without calling Image._decompression_bomb_check(), allowing a crafted .gd file to trigger excessive C-heap allocation when loaded. This issue is fixed in version 12.3.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-55380",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-55380\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: Pillow\nFixed Version: 12.3.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-55380](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-55380)\nPillow is a Python imaging library. Prior to 12.3.0, PIL/GdImageFile.py GdImageFile._open() read image dimensions from the GD 2.x header and stored them in self._size without calling Image._decompression_bomb_check(), allowing a crafted .gd file to trigger excessive C-heap allocation when loaded. This issue is fixed in version 12.3.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-55380**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|Pillow|12.3.0|[CVE-2026-55380](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-55380)|\n\nPillow is a Python imaging library. Prior to 12.3.0, PIL/GdImageFile.py GdImageFile._open() read image dimensions from the GD 2.x header and stored them in self._size without calling Image._decompression_bomb_check(), allowing a crafted .gd file to trigger excessive C-heap allocation when loaded. This issue is fixed in version 12.3.0."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
